{
 "about": "The platform features scripts/browser-support.mjs looks for in each element's code and CSS (and in tokens.css, which every element reads), with the first browser versions that support them. Versions are MDN browser-compat-data (bcd key on each row) – checked against @mdn/browser-compat-data 8.1.7 on 2026-10-27; `node scripts/browser-support.mjs --bcd` re-reads them. null: no version supports it. `pattern` is a regular expression run on the source with comments removed; `alt` is an older or prefixed form that, when the same code also has it, lowers the versions; `progressive` features have a fallback and say what changes without them; `watch` features aren't used by any element yet – the scanner reports them as soon as one does (tests/browser-features.test.ts).",
 "bcd": "8.1.7",
 "checked": "2026-10-27",
 "features": [
  {
   "id": "light-dark",
   "name": "light-dark()",
   "bcd": "css.types.color.light-dark",
   "pattern": "light-dark\\(",
   "sample": "--tc-text: light-dark(#111, #eee);",
   "versions": {
    "chrome": "123",
    "edge": "123",
    "firefox": "120",
    "safari": "17.5",
    "safari_ios": "17.5"
   },
   "why": "Every colour token is a light / dark pair; without it no colour token resolves."
  },
  {
